MANIFEST

# Per-project virtualenvs
.venv*/
.conda*/
venv*/*

# Jupyter files
*checkpoint.ipynb

# Generated figures
# Plots are derived artifacts — regenerate them from the tracked .csv rather
# than storing them. The run plots under output/ are handled by output/.gitignore,
# which is deny-all and simply stops re-including *.png; this rule covers
# everywhere else. docs/ images are hand-written documentation, so keep those.
# Adding a genuinely new figure elsewhere needs `git add -f`.
*.png
!docs/*.png

# Real-robot deployment binaries (handover_sim2real/sim2real/)
# The sim2real SOURCE is tracked — policy_runner.py, camera.py, the calibration
# scripts and their small .npy/.json. These are the payloads that came with it:
# 454 MB of .ckpt, 630 MB of RealSense .bag, 15 MB of rendered .mp4. GitHub
# hard-rejects anything over 100 MB, and git keeps blobs forever, so a later
# delete would not shrink the history.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored: checkpoint/*/config.yaml and normalization.npz.
# Those are ~1 KB and are the ONLY record of how to denormalize a checkpoint's
# output — same reasoning as the run npz under output/.gitignore.
*.ckpt
*.bag
*.mp4
# WEIGHTS, ANYWHERE — not just under sim2real/checkpoint/. That path-anchored
# rule is why a 149 MB SAM2 checkpoint reached the index: a bad cwd created a
# duplicate package tree at sim2real/handover_sim2real/sim2real/checkpoint/sam2/,
# which has an extra `handover_sim2real/sim2real/` in the middle and so matched
# nothing. An unanchored rule cannot be dodged by where the file lands, and a
# binary that size is effectively permanent — deleting it in a later commit
# leaves it in history and every clone still pays for it.
#
# The small files BESIDE a checkpoint stay tracked (config.yaml,
# normalization.npz, README.md, source.txt): the payload does not carry the
# Normalizer and the .h5 it was fitted on lives on /scratch, so those are the
# only record of how to denormalize a policy's output.
*.pt
*.pth
*.safetensors

# The stray duplicate package tree itself. It holds nothing but the checkpoint
# above; the real tree is at the repo root.
handover_sim2real/sim2real/handover_sim2real/

# SLURM job output. `*.log` near the top of this file does not match .out/.err.
slurm_logs/
*.out
*.err

output_home_shards/
